Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: How accurate must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard)\nOption B: Accurate in all material respects\nOption C: Accurate in all respects\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 8.3 Conditions to Obligations of Acquirer and Acquisition Sub. The obligations of Acquirer and Acquisition Sub to consummate the Closing are subject to the satisfaction, or waiver by Acquirer, prior to the Closing of the following conditions: (a) Representations and Warranties. (i) The representations and warranties of the Target set forth in Sections 4.1(a), 4.1(b), and 4.2 shall be true and correct in all respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date as if made on and as of the Closing Date, except for inaccuracies that are de minimis in nature. (ii) The representations and warranties of the Target set forth in Sections 4.3 and 4.4 shall be true and correct in all material respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date as if made on and as of the Closing Date, except where the failure to be so true and correct would not, individually or in the aggregate, have a Material Adverse Effect on the Target. (iii) All other representations and warranties of the Target contained in this Agreement shall be true and correct in all respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date as if made on and as of the Closing Date, except for any inaccuracies that, individually or in the aggregate, would not have a Material Adverse Effect on the Target or the Surviving Entity. (Page 85)\nAnswer:
